WEBVTT

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.136
It's all right, Chief.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.969
You're going to be just fine.

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.134
What happened?

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.575
You were rerouting
a phase inducer

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.875
when one of the plasma conduits
blew out.

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.312
Oh.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:16.315
Easy there, Chief.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.943
You've got a mild case
of radiation poisoning.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.782
I'll give you some hyronalin

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.412
which should
counteract the effects

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.888
but I do think
he should be restricted

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.288
to light duty
for the next few days.

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.792
Agreed.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.886
Commander,
the transport's arrived

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.556
and they're requesting
permission to dock.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.327
Route them to Docking Bay 12.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.927
Inform the Romulan Delegation
we'll meet them there.

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.699
And Chief, "light duty"
means light.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.301
I don't want to see you
crawling around

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:48.212
the Jefferies tube tonight
looking for power surges.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:51.979
You won't get any arguments
today, Commander.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:53.610
Ready, Major?

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:07.230
Promenade.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.106
Du'cha KovaH!

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.373
EstaH! EstaH!

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.879
Constable, I wasn't aware

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.280
there were any Klingons
on the station.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:26.114
They just arrived
a few hours ago.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.246
It seems the main computer
on their freighter was damaged

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.382
and they need
a complete overhaul

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.655
before they can continue
back to the Klingon Empire.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.161
How long is this overhaul
going to take?

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.526
Two days, at least.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.930
The Romulan delegation
has just arrived

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.565
and they're going to be here
at least two days

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.939
while they study
our intelligence reports

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.341
on the Dominion.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.470
I want you to keep a close eye
on the Klingons.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.140
We don't need
any trouble right now.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.148
Understood.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.444
Let's go.

00:01:57.484 --> 00:01:59.384
Come on.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.773
Welcome to Deep Space 9.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:28.304
I'm Commander Sisko, and this is
my First Officer, Major Kira.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.814
I am Ruwon.
This is Karina.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.979
We are ready for your report
on the Dominion.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.318
We have arranged
quarters for you.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:38.551
I know it's been a long trip,
so perhaps you'd like to...

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.580
We are not interested

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.093
in your accommodations,
Commander.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.992
We are here for
your intelligence briefing...

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.495
nothing else.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.125
Very well.

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.433
If you'll come this way.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.371
This will be the foul line.

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.211
We need to put a marker
here on the floor.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.375
I still don't see

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.578
how this is going to help
my business, Chief.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.917
No, that's not right.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.651
The number 20 needs
to be at the top.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.522
Trust me, Quark.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.461
Darts and bars go together
like bacon and eggs.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.657
At least people order
bacon and eggs.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:20.529
In all the years
I've been here,

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.695
no one has ever come
and asked to see the dart board.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.964
Trust me, they will.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.666
I just don't see
the appeal of this game.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:31.505
No lasers, no holograms.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:34.945
Just steel tips and feathers.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.812
It's a game of skill, Quark.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:38.111
And it's not easy.

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.379
Go ahead.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.511
Try and get one
in the bull's-eye.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.749
No!

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.798
Now what if one of those darts
had gotten into his eye?

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.993
Do you realize
I'd be liable for that?

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.467
Do you know how much
money an eye costs?

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.698
You're not supposed
to throw them like that.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:02.640
You throw them gently.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.142
One at a time.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:05.405
Like this.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.783
Chief O'Brien.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:11.943
What is it, Quark?

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:12.952
The Klingons

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.647
just destroyed
two of my holosuites.

00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:16.450
I need a maintenance crew
immediately.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:17.649
Quark, this happens

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.715
every time the Klingons
come aboard the station.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.920
Why don't you just keep
them out of the holosuites?

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:24.191
Did you ever say no
to a Klingon?

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.391
Besides, they pay me double.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.306
Chief?

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.503
Chief!

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:39.594
Well, the pain you experienced
appears to be a muscle spasm

00:06:39.631 --> 00:06:42.862
caused by a sudden decrease
in your serum calcium levels.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:46.302
It's a common side effect
of radiation poisoning.

00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:48.806
I'm giving you some
asinolyathin for the pain.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.468
What about the vision I had?

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.068
Well, mild hallucinations

00:06:53.111 --> 00:06:55.477
are also a fairly
common side effect

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:56.981
of radiation poisoning.

00:06:57.015 --> 00:06:59.142
It was anything but mild.

00:06:59.184 --> 00:07:03.211
I really felt
I was standing on the Promenade

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.723
watching myself
talking to Quark.

00:07:05.757 --> 00:07:07.315
What was the conversation about?

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:09.919
He was complaining
about some Klingons.

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:13.898
He said they'd damaged
two of his holosuites.

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:16.799
Well, you do have one problem.

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:19.326
If all you can hallucinate about
is Quark's maintenance problems

00:07:19.371 --> 00:07:20.998
you have a sadly
deficient fantasy life.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.268
Well, thank you
for your professional opinion.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.538
Oh, any time.

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:28.705
My doors are always open to you,
Chief.

00:07:30.215 --> 00:07:32.740
The Dominion represents
the greatest threat

00:07:32.784 --> 00:07:34.945
to the Alpha Quadrant
in the last century.

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.956
We need more information
on its military capabilities.

00:07:38.056 --> 00:07:39.546
How many ships do they have?

00:07:39.591 --> 00:07:40.922
Where are they deployed?

00:07:40.959 --> 00:07:43.120
What are their plans
for the future?

00:07:43.161 --> 00:07:44.651
Are they planning an attack?

00:07:44.696 --> 00:07:46.254
We don't know any of that yet.

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:47.526
You have one of Founders

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:49.557
of the Dominion
on this very station.

00:07:49.601 --> 00:07:52.126
He should be able to tell us
everything we need to know

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.228
about their intentions.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.331
Odo is not one of the Founders.

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:56.568
Your own reports indicate

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:58.508
that a group of changelings
are the real

00:07:58.543 --> 00:08:00.272
source of power
behind the Dominion.

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:01.301
Yes.

00:08:01.346 --> 00:08:02.711
And Odo is a changeling.

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:04.579
But he's not
one of the Founders.

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:07.676
I fail to see the distinction.

00:08:07.719 --> 00:08:10.415
Odo made a conscious choice
to stay here with us.

00:08:10.455 --> 00:08:12.389
He has no loyalties
to the Dominion

00:08:12.424 --> 00:08:15.086
and he has no information
about their plans.

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:17.118
We find that hard to believe.

00:08:17.162 --> 00:08:20.563
It's the truth, whether you
choose to believe it or not.

00:08:32.878 --> 00:08:34.243
Commander, we allowed you

00:08:34.279 --> 00:08:37.077
to place one of our cloaking
devices on the Defiant

00:08:37.115 --> 00:08:39.913
in exchange for information
regarding the Dominion.

00:08:39.951 --> 00:08:45.446
Now you have the cloaking device
and we have very little.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:48.721
We shouldn't have to remind you
of the importance

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:50.421
both our governments place

00:08:50.462 --> 00:08:52.487
on continuing to carry out
this agreement.

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:53.896
It's the first treaty

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:56.901
between Romulus and
the Federation in many years.

00:08:56.935 --> 00:08:58.266
I'm aware of that

00:08:58.303 --> 00:09:01.466
and I'm willing to cooperate
with you in any way I can.

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:02.530
Very well, then.

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:05.270
We want to see
every piece of information

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:09.269
Starfleet has on the Dominion,
no matter how insignificant.

00:09:09.314 --> 00:09:10.838
That includes
any classified reports

00:09:10.882 --> 00:09:12.577
you may have made
to Starfleet Command.

00:09:12.617 --> 00:09:14.448
I'll have to clear that
with Starfleet.

00:09:14.486 --> 00:09:15.976
Then do it.

00:09:29.401 --> 00:09:31.266
Chief O'Brien.

00:09:31.303 --> 00:09:32.565
What is it, Quark?

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:35.630
The Klingons just destroyed
two of my holosuites.

00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:37.539
I need a maintenance crew
immediately.

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.168
Quark, we go through this

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:41.941
every time Klingons
come aboard the station.

00:09:42.013 --> 00:09:43.913
Why don't you ju...?

00:09:49.554 --> 00:09:51.784
I think my holosuites
can wait.

00:09:51.823 --> 00:09:54.724
It looks like you have
bigger problems.

00:10:01.299 --> 00:10:03.130
I went over
the internal sensor logs

00:10:03.168 --> 00:10:04.362
and I did find evidence

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:06.428
of a minor temporal
disturbance in Quark's

00:10:06.471 --> 00:10:09.565
and another one later,
on the Promenade.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:11.769
Both disturbances happened
at about the same time

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:12.902
as the Chief's experiences.

00:10:12.944 --> 00:10:14.172
So, it would seem

00:10:14.212 --> 00:10:16.339
that you did travel
into the future

00:10:16.381 --> 00:10:18.781
and then returned
to the same moment

00:10:18.817 --> 00:10:20.250
that you left.

00:10:20.285 --> 00:10:24.688
Have you any idea what might
have caused this time shift?

00:10:24.723 --> 00:10:25.815
Not yet.

00:10:25.857 --> 00:10:27.688
I want to go over
the medical scans

00:10:27.726 --> 00:10:29.159
Julian took of you earlier.

00:10:29.194 --> 00:10:31.560
That dose of ionizing
radiation you received

00:10:31.596 --> 00:10:34.087
might have something
to do with it.

00:10:34.132 --> 00:10:35.326
How?

00:10:35.367 --> 00:10:37.801
I'm not sure,
but it's a good place to start.

00:10:37.836 --> 00:10:39.463
I have heard
a couple of theories

00:10:39.504 --> 00:10:42.302
that ambient low-level radiation
could have a temporal...

00:11:09.534 --> 00:11:10.523
Look out!

00:11:12.003 --> 00:11:14.335
...effect
on radioactive isotopes.

00:11:17.175 --> 00:11:18.836
Chief!

00:11:20.078 --> 00:11:21.636
Mr. O'Brien.

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:31.215
I ran a microcellular scan

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:32.382
and detected minute damage

00:11:32.424 --> 00:11:33.789
to his cerebrospinal
nerve cells

00:11:33.825 --> 00:11:35.986
which might have been caused
by the timeshifting.

00:11:36.027 --> 00:11:37.153
Can you repair it?

00:11:37.195 --> 00:11:38.594
Yes, but the effect
is cumulative.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.655
If you keep timeshifting,
there may come a point

00:11:40.699 --> 00:11:42.257
where the damage
becomes irreparable.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.063
Eventually, it might
even kill you.

00:11:45.303 --> 00:11:46.964
Don't worry, Chief...
Dax is using

00:11:47.005 --> 00:11:48.336
every scanner on the station

00:11:48.373 --> 00:11:50.273
to hunt for any temporal
abnormalities.

00:11:50.308 --> 00:11:53.141
Well, if anyone
can find the cause

00:11:53.178 --> 00:11:55.669
of the time shifts, it's Dax.

00:11:55.714 --> 00:11:57.841
Chief, do you have any idea
of how far into the future

00:11:57.883 --> 00:11:58.850
you traveled?

00:11:58.884 --> 00:11:59.942
No, sir.

00:11:59.985 --> 00:12:02.954
There was nothing to indicate
that it was today

00:12:03.021 --> 00:12:04.318
tomorrow, next week.

00:12:04.356 --> 00:12:06.688
Well, this conference
with the Romulans

00:12:06.725 --> 00:12:09.489
is not supposed to last
longer than three days.

00:12:09.528 --> 00:12:13.157
In the meantime, I'll have Odo
tighten security around Quark's.

00:12:13.198 --> 00:12:14.825
How are you feeling, Chief?

00:12:14.866 --> 00:12:15.833
Better.

00:12:15.867 --> 00:12:16.856
Good.

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:19.564
Commander, may I speak with you
for a minute?

00:12:19.604 --> 00:12:20.730
Of course.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.171
The Romulans want
to debrief everyone

00:12:27.212 --> 00:12:28.179
who was on the Defiant

00:12:28.213 --> 00:12:29.646
when it was captured
by the Founders.

00:12:29.681 --> 00:12:30.978
They're also still not happy

00:12:31.049 --> 00:12:33.517
with the sensor information
collected by the Defiant

00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:36.282
so they want unrestricted
access to the Defiant

00:12:36.321 --> 00:12:37.515
and they also want

00:12:37.556 --> 00:12:39.421
complete access
to all our personal logs.

00:12:39.457 --> 00:12:41.391
Personal logs are
out of the question

00:12:41.426 --> 00:12:44.088
but they can have limited
access to the Defiant.

00:12:44.129 --> 00:12:45.790
I'll let them
debrief us, as well.

00:12:46.965 --> 00:12:48.626
I know they're pushing us, Major

00:12:48.667 --> 00:12:50.134
but consider their position.

00:12:50.168 --> 00:12:51.465
There have never been
any Romulan ships

00:12:51.503 --> 00:12:52.704
in the Gamma Quadrant

00:12:52.837 --> 00:12:54.464
so they've never
encountered the Dominion.

00:12:54.505 --> 00:12:56.837
So they're completely dependent
on us for information.

00:12:56.874 --> 00:12:59.001
Well, then maybe they should
send their own ships

00:12:59.043 --> 00:13:01.204
through the wormhole
and find out for themselves.

00:13:01.245 --> 00:13:03.110
The Romulans generally
prefer to sit back

00:13:03.147 --> 00:13:05.547
and pull the strings from
a distance, if they can.

00:13:05.583 --> 00:13:07.551
This is one puppet who doesn't
like her strings pulled.

00:13:07.585 --> 00:13:08.950
I know, but like Ruwon said

00:13:09.053 --> 00:13:11.613
they've lived up
to their part of the bargain.

00:13:11.656 --> 00:13:14.454
We have to do everything we can
to live up to ours.

00:13:14.492 --> 00:13:16.187
All right, I'll draw up
a schedule of interviews

00:13:16.227 --> 00:13:17.524
and I'll tell everyone
to cooperate.

00:13:17.562 --> 00:13:19.860
And, Major, when you're
with the Romulans

00:13:19.897 --> 00:13:21.865
try to be diplomatic.

00:13:21.899 --> 00:13:23.730
I'm always diplomatic.

00:13:25.436 --> 00:13:27.666
That is the most ridiculous
thing I ever heard

00:13:27.705 --> 00:13:29.138
and I resent the implication.

00:13:29.173 --> 00:13:30.435
You seem very agitated

00:13:30.475 --> 00:13:33.137
for someone who's
proclaiming her innocence.

00:13:33.177 --> 00:13:36.237
Indeed, your emotional state
would seem to indicate

00:13:36.280 --> 00:13:37.838
that our theory is correct

00:13:37.882 --> 00:13:40.578
and you did abandon
the Defiant prematurely

00:13:40.618 --> 00:13:42.745
when it was attacked
by the Jem'Hadar.

00:13:46.858 --> 00:13:48.689
When the Defiant was attacked

00:13:48.726 --> 00:13:50.956
Odo and I were
trapped below decks.

00:13:50.995 --> 00:13:53.987
There was a hand-to-hand
fight in the corridor.

00:13:54.098 --> 00:13:56.623
I was wounded,
and I lost consciousness.

00:13:56.667 --> 00:13:58.999
When I came to,
Odo had already put me

00:13:59.103 --> 00:14:01.469
aboard the shuttle,
and we'd escaped.

00:14:01.506 --> 00:14:04.304
I did not abandon
the ship prematurely.

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:08.736
Why didn't Odo try to help
the rest of the Defiant's crew?

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.179
Well, I'm sure he wanted to

00:14:10.214 --> 00:14:12.705
but there was no way
to get to the Bridge, and...

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:15.913
Why were you in Odo's quarters
when the ship was attacked?

00:14:15.953 --> 00:14:17.614
We were talking.

00:14:17.655 --> 00:14:18.815
About what?

00:14:18.856 --> 00:14:20.187
It's personal.

00:14:20.224 --> 00:14:21.748
Do you often have

00:14:21.793 --> 00:14:23.818
personal talks
with the changeling?

00:14:23.861 --> 00:14:27.262
What business is that of yours?

00:14:27.298 --> 00:14:29.698
We're trying to determine the
nature of your relationship.

00:14:29.734 --> 00:14:31.201
You are the only member

00:14:31.235 --> 00:14:33.499
of the Defiant's crew
who was not taken prisoner.

00:14:33.538 --> 00:14:34.505
Why?

00:14:34.539 --> 00:14:37.201
Did the Founders believe
Odo would react badly

00:14:37.241 --> 00:14:38.674
if you were harmed?

00:14:38.709 --> 00:14:41.872
Did they think you held
some kind of attraction to him?

00:14:41.913 --> 00:14:45.178
Has Odo ever shown any kind
of physical interest

00:14:45.216 --> 00:14:46.581
in you, Major?

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.082
That's it.

00:14:50.121 --> 00:14:52.351
You can rip the cloaking device

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.085
out of the Defiant right now!

00:14:54.125 --> 00:14:56.958
I am not answering
any more questions.

00:14:56.994 --> 00:14:59.861
And I suggest you avoid
asking Odo those questions

00:14:59.897 --> 00:15:01.558
or you may just find yourself

00:15:01.599 --> 00:15:04.466
on the other side
of that bulkhead, floating home.

00:15:17.982 --> 00:15:19.950
There.
That's the game.

00:15:20.051 --> 00:15:21.211
Had enough?

00:15:21.252 --> 00:15:22.844
One more.

00:15:22.887 --> 00:15:25.947
Chief, that's the tenth game
we've played in a row.

00:15:26.057 --> 00:15:27.183
Nothing's happening here

00:15:27.225 --> 00:15:29.420
and I don't think anything
is going to happen.

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:31.826
By telling us about the fight,
you have changed the future.

00:15:31.863 --> 00:15:33.421
Security's here, and Quark says

00:15:33.464 --> 00:15:35.125
he won't let the Klingons
back in the bar.

00:15:35.166 --> 00:15:36.497
There is not going
to be a fight.

00:15:36.534 --> 00:15:40.630
I know, I know, but...

00:15:40.671 --> 00:15:44.300
I've seen it, and I
can't shake the feeling

00:15:44.342 --> 00:15:45.866
that it's going to happen

00:15:45.910 --> 00:15:47.741
despite our precautions.

00:15:47.778 --> 00:15:49.507
Something about
the way things look

00:15:49.547 --> 00:15:50.605
the number of people.

00:15:50.648 --> 00:15:52.513
There's something
a little too familiar

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.983
about everything.

00:15:54.018 --> 00:15:56.486
All right, if it makes
you feel any better

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.613
I'll beat you
at another ten games.

00:15:58.656 --> 00:16:00.146
But I can't help
getting the feeling...

00:16:02.193 --> 00:16:04.388
Ach'cho korvak bataH!

00:16:04.428 --> 00:16:05.827
Karagh, abeH.

00:16:13.204 --> 00:16:14.398
You said you weren't
going to let

00:16:14.438 --> 00:16:15.530
the Klingons back in the bar!

00:16:15.573 --> 00:16:17.097
I didn't.

00:16:17.141 --> 00:16:18.699
They were in the holosuites.

00:16:18.743 --> 00:16:22.179
Besides, now they're
paying me triple.

00:16:36.661 --> 00:16:39.221
Who let these filthy pahtk
in here?

00:16:39.263 --> 00:16:41.697
Maybe we should
show them the way out.

00:16:44.502 --> 00:16:46.231
And then...

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:47.703
What's his name?

00:16:47.738 --> 00:16:49.069
Ruwon?

00:16:49.106 --> 00:16:52.303
Ruwon started to insinuate
that...

00:16:52.343 --> 00:16:53.367
you were...

00:16:53.411 --> 00:16:55.174
That I was what?

00:16:55.212 --> 00:16:57.476
Interested in me.

00:16:57.515 --> 00:16:58.504
He said that?

00:16:58.549 --> 00:17:00.642
Have you ever heard
anything more...

00:17:00.685 --> 00:17:01.652
Ridiculous!

00:17:01.686 --> 00:17:02.653
Exactly.

00:17:02.687 --> 00:17:03.654
Quark to Security.

00:17:03.688 --> 00:17:05.212
I've got a fight on my hands.

00:17:05.256 --> 00:17:06.951
They're tearing my place apart.

00:17:28.479 --> 00:17:30.106
Watch the Romulan!

00:17:31.983 --> 00:17:33.712
All right, that's enough!

00:17:33.751 --> 00:17:34.718
Get back!

00:17:34.752 --> 00:17:36.219
Come on!

00:17:37.421 --> 00:17:38.752
Move it.
Move it.

00:17:38.789 --> 00:17:40.654
Let's go.
Come on now.

00:17:47.631 --> 00:17:48.928
Miles?

00:18:15.359 --> 00:18:17.054
Chief.

00:18:17.094 --> 00:18:18.152
It's all right.

00:18:18.195 --> 00:18:20.220
You collapsed outside Quark's
about an hour ago.

00:18:20.264 --> 00:18:21.925
You're going to be fine.

00:18:21.999 --> 00:18:23.466
No, I'm not.

00:18:23.501 --> 00:18:26.959
In a few hours,
I'm going to be dead.

00:18:33.978 --> 00:18:36.845
This is the panel
I saw myself open.

00:18:36.881 --> 00:18:39.748
It looked like a phaser
or high-energy laser

00:18:39.784 --> 00:18:41.649
came out of the bulkhead.

00:18:41.685 --> 00:18:43.050
Nothing on the tricorder.

00:18:43.087 --> 00:18:46.113
Just the standard conduits
and power juncture ports.

00:18:46.157 --> 00:18:48.625
If there is something
dangerous in there

00:18:48.659 --> 00:18:49.683
it could be cloaked

00:18:49.727 --> 00:18:52.287
or have some dampening field
around it.

00:18:52.329 --> 00:18:54.058
If you gentlemen will
step down the corridor

00:18:54.098 --> 00:18:56.430
I'll open the panel
and take a look.

00:18:56.467 --> 00:18:58.367
Don't worry.
I'll be careful.

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.160
It's all right.

00:19:25.196 --> 00:19:26.891
Nothing.

00:19:26.931 --> 00:19:29.229
You're sure
this is the right panel?

00:19:29.266 --> 00:19:30.324
Absolutely.

00:19:30.367 --> 00:19:32.699
Believe me,
I've a pretty vivid memory

00:19:32.736 --> 00:19:33.964
of the whole thing.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:40.406
Well... since it appears
that your first two time jumps

00:19:40.444 --> 00:19:42.935
each moved you to about
five hours into the future

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:44.106
we could also assume

00:19:44.148 --> 00:19:46.776
that the incident
you saw in this corridor

00:19:46.817 --> 00:19:49.718
moved you to about five hours
into the future.

00:19:49.753 --> 00:19:51.948
That means someone
will place a device

00:19:51.989 --> 00:19:54.124
in this panel
in the next few hours.

00:19:54.257 --> 00:19:57.715
All these quarters
are vacant at the moment.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:00.888
There are no vital power
conduits in this area.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:02.727
No crucial defense systems.

00:20:02.765 --> 00:20:04.756
Why would someone
want to booby-trap

00:20:04.801 --> 00:20:05.825
a wall panel here?

00:20:05.869 --> 00:20:08.929
I suggest we place
a surveillance device

00:20:08.972 --> 00:20:10.303
in this corridor.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:12.331
If anyone attempts
to tamper with the panel

00:20:12.375 --> 00:20:13.706
we'll be able to detect it.

00:20:14.844 --> 00:20:16.778
Dax to Sisko.

00:20:16.813 --> 00:20:18.303
Sisko here.
Go ahead, Lieutenant.

00:20:18.348 --> 00:20:20.179
Benjamin,
can you come to Ops?

00:20:20.216 --> 00:20:23.947
I think I've found a clue
to Chief O'Brien's timeshifting.

00:20:23.987 --> 00:20:25.454
We're on our way.

00:20:25.488 --> 00:20:27.012
Keep me informed.

00:20:31.861 --> 00:20:33.829
I've been scanning the area
around the station

00:20:33.863 --> 00:20:35.592
out to a radius
of two kilometers.

00:20:35.632 --> 00:20:37.327
I didn't find anything at first.

00:20:37.367 --> 00:20:41.235
Then I started to scan some of
the lower subspace bandwidths.

00:20:41.271 --> 00:20:44.172
I found traces of low-level
tetryon emissions.

00:20:44.207 --> 00:20:46.004
I've never seen
an emission pattern

00:20:46.075 --> 00:20:48.009
like that
outside of a neutron star.

00:20:48.044 --> 00:20:49.636
Or a quantum singularity.

00:20:49.679 --> 00:20:51.738
And singularities are
known to send out waves

00:20:51.781 --> 00:20:52.975
of temporal displacement.

00:20:53.016 --> 00:20:54.984
But if there is
a singularity nearby

00:20:55.018 --> 00:20:56.246
why can't we find it?

00:20:56.286 --> 00:20:59.847
It should also be affecting the
gravimetric field signatures.

00:20:59.889 --> 00:21:00.878
I don't know.

00:21:00.924 --> 00:21:02.357
Maybe it's buried so far down

00:21:02.392 --> 00:21:04.792
in the subspace layers
that we can't detect it.

00:21:04.827 --> 00:21:06.351
Assuming for the moment

00:21:06.396 --> 00:21:08.796
that a singularity
is responsible

00:21:08.831 --> 00:21:11.129
how do we combat
its effects on the Chief?

00:21:11.167 --> 00:21:14.603
Temporal displacement
caused by a quantum singularity

00:21:14.637 --> 00:21:18.573
most commonly affects
delta-series radioisotopes

00:21:18.608 --> 00:21:20.098
which is exactly
what the Chief absorbed

00:21:20.143 --> 00:21:21.167
during the conduit breach.

00:21:21.211 --> 00:21:22.405
So you're saying that it

00:21:22.445 --> 00:21:24.811
could be pulling O'Brien's body
like a magnet?

00:21:24.847 --> 00:21:26.144
Exactly.

00:21:26.182 --> 00:21:29.276
I think I may know a way
to neutralize the remaining

00:21:29.319 --> 00:21:30.547
radioisotopes in your body.

00:21:30.587 --> 00:21:32.282
Without the radiation

00:21:32.322 --> 00:21:34.256
the temporal displacement
might stop.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:35.348
It's going to take time.

00:21:35.391 --> 00:21:37.951
You may experience
one or two more time shifts

00:21:37.994 --> 00:21:39.985
before I can
complete the process.

00:21:40.029 --> 00:21:40.996
When can we start?

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:42.054
Right away.

00:21:48.004 --> 00:21:49.995
Keep trying to pinpoint
the singularity.

00:21:50.039 --> 00:21:51.939
If it is out there,
we need to locate it

00:21:51.975 --> 00:21:53.533
and find a way to get rid of it.

00:21:53.576 --> 00:21:55.168
Right.

00:21:57.847 --> 00:21:58.814
I wanted to let you know

00:21:58.848 --> 00:22:00.475
I moved the Romulans
to different quarters.

00:22:00.516 --> 00:22:01.483
Oh?

00:22:01.517 --> 00:22:02.643
It's the replicators again.

00:22:02.685 --> 00:22:03.947
I assigned a maintenance crew.

00:22:03.987 --> 00:22:06.114
But in the meantime, I moved
the entire Romulan delegation

00:22:06.155 --> 00:22:10.285
to section 47, level 2
in the Habitat Ring.

00:22:10.326 --> 00:22:11.452
Section 47?

00:22:11.494 --> 00:22:12.654
Yes.
Is something wrong?

00:22:12.695 --> 00:22:16.222
The wall panel where O'Brien
saw himself being killed

00:22:16.266 --> 00:22:18.461
is right outside those quarters.

00:22:19.669 --> 00:22:21.694
Which means either the Romulans

00:22:21.738 --> 00:22:25.105
are going to put a device
in the bulkhead themselves

00:22:25.141 --> 00:22:26.472
or someone else will

00:22:26.509 --> 00:22:28.909
possibly to be used
against the Romulans.

00:22:28.945 --> 00:22:31.379
Should I move them
to other quarters?

00:22:31.414 --> 00:22:33.712
No. That'll warn
whoever is responsible.

00:22:33.750 --> 00:22:36.514
But inform Odo
of the change in quarters.

00:22:36.552 --> 00:22:40.488
He already has that corridor
under surveillance.

00:22:40.523 --> 00:22:42.491
Let's see
how this thing plays out

00:22:42.525 --> 00:22:44.493
before we make
any further moves.

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:52.224
You have something, Constable?

00:22:52.268 --> 00:22:55.669
Someone has planted
a class-3 surveillance device

00:22:55.705 --> 00:22:58.674
behind the wall panel
we've been monitoring.

00:22:58.708 --> 00:23:01.108
Were you able to see who it was?

00:23:01.144 --> 00:23:03.840
No, we've been monitoring
the corridor constantly

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:05.313
for the past three hours.

00:23:05.348 --> 00:23:07.441
No one's come anywhere
near the panel.

00:23:07.483 --> 00:23:10.043
However, sensors did detect

00:23:10.086 --> 00:23:14.614
a low-energy transporter beam
a short time ago.

00:23:14.657 --> 00:23:19.287
They beamed the device
directly into the wall.

00:23:19.329 --> 00:23:22.890
That's a delicate piece
of transporter work.

00:23:22.932 --> 00:23:24.729
Yes, it is.

00:23:24.767 --> 00:23:28.294
We haven't been able
to trace the beam

00:23:28.338 --> 00:23:29.703
to its point of origin

00:23:29.739 --> 00:23:31.730
but since there aren't
any ships nearby

00:23:31.774 --> 00:23:34.242
I believe it originated
on the station.

00:23:34.277 --> 00:23:35.301
Any suspects?

00:23:36.346 --> 00:23:39.144
Well, since it appears
to be a device

00:23:39.182 --> 00:23:41.377
intended to conduct
covert surveillance

00:23:41.417 --> 00:23:42.406
of the Romulans

00:23:42.452 --> 00:23:44.852
my leading suspects
would be the Klingons.

00:23:44.887 --> 00:23:45.979
Do you have any evidence

00:23:46.089 --> 00:23:48.284
besides the fact that Klingons
hate Romulans?

00:23:48.324 --> 00:23:50.656
Well, not yet, but don't worry.

00:23:50.693 --> 00:23:53.662
I plan to investigate
the Klingons

00:23:53.696 --> 00:23:57.257
the Bajorans, Quark,
the visiting Terrellians...

00:23:57.300 --> 00:23:59.825
You think Quark
had something to do with this?

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:03.402
I always investigate Quark.

00:24:11.013 --> 00:24:13.675
Looks like you're going
to cheat death, after all.

00:24:13.716 --> 00:24:16.378
Round about this time,
you saw yourself being killed.

00:24:16.419 --> 00:24:20.685
I feel like someone
just walked over my grave.

00:24:20.723 --> 00:24:23.658
I mean, I've had a few brushes
with death in my career

00:24:23.693 --> 00:24:25.126
but there was something

00:24:25.161 --> 00:24:27.391
about watching
myself being killed...

00:24:27.430 --> 00:24:31.127
of feeling my own neck
for a pulse that wasn't there.

00:24:31.167 --> 00:24:35.126
Well, could have been worse.

00:24:35.171 --> 00:24:36.968
Could have been me.

00:24:38.741 --> 00:24:40.732
Here you are, gentlemen.

00:24:40.777 --> 00:24:45.180
And how is DS9's
most famous fortune teller?

00:24:45.214 --> 00:24:46.977
Don't call me that.

00:24:47.016 --> 00:24:49.143
I haven't told anyone's fortune.

00:24:49.185 --> 00:24:51.415
Oh, just a figure of speech.

00:24:51.454 --> 00:24:53.615
On the other hand

00:24:53.656 --> 00:24:56.557
if you should find yourself
in the future again

00:24:56.592 --> 00:24:59.686
and you find yourself
passing by the dabo table

00:24:59.729 --> 00:25:02.789
would it really hurt
to take a look

00:25:02.832 --> 00:25:04.891
at the numbers
coming up on the wheel?

00:25:04.934 --> 00:25:08.631
I could make it
worth your while.

00:25:08.671 --> 00:25:11.231
Let's get out of here.

00:25:14.710 --> 00:25:16.268
Just a thought.

00:25:18.414 --> 00:25:20.109
Can you believe that?

00:25:20.149 --> 00:25:22.344
I'm being pulled into the future
and all he can think about is...

00:25:56.519 --> 00:25:57.986
Chief!

00:25:58.054 --> 00:26:00.420
Oh, am I glad to see you.

00:26:00.456 --> 00:26:02.117
What the hell
happened to me, Julian?

00:26:02.158 --> 00:26:03.591
It was the, the radiation.

00:26:03.626 --> 00:26:06.459
I didn't realize it had
damaged the basilar arteries

00:26:06.496 --> 00:26:08.691
in your brain stem
until it was too late.

00:26:08.731 --> 00:26:09.720
Well, why not?

00:26:09.765 --> 00:26:11.699
It didn't show up
on any of the diagnostics.

00:26:11.734 --> 00:26:13.031
I couldn't tell
what had happened

00:26:13.069 --> 00:26:14.331
until I was doing the autopsy.

00:26:14.370 --> 00:26:15.928
Autopsy.

00:26:15.972 --> 00:26:17.872
Yeah, I just finished
doing it a few moments ago.

00:26:17.907 --> 00:26:19.431
Do you want me
to show you the results?

00:26:19.475 --> 00:26:20.464
No, no, no!

00:26:20.510 --> 00:26:22.501
That's, that's all right.

00:26:22.545 --> 00:26:25.105
Now, look, when you go
back to the past

00:26:25.147 --> 00:26:28.378
ask me to perform
a basilar arterial scan

00:26:28.417 --> 00:26:30.317
and since you're going
five hours back into the past

00:26:30.353 --> 00:26:31.581
I should have enough time

00:26:31.621 --> 00:26:33.748
to find the damage
and repair it before...

00:26:33.789 --> 00:26:35.586
this happens.

00:26:35.625 --> 00:26:37.286
Right.

00:26:40.329 --> 00:26:43.560
How could you just let me die?

00:26:43.599 --> 00:26:45.430
I didn't just let you die.

00:26:45.468 --> 00:26:46.799
I did everything I could

00:26:46.836 --> 00:26:48.736
to keep you alive
for over an hour

00:26:48.771 --> 00:26:50.261
but your body just gave up.

00:26:50.306 --> 00:26:51.739
Gave up?

00:26:51.774 --> 00:26:54.242
I'm sorry, Chief.

00:26:54.277 --> 00:26:55.608
But there comes a point

00:26:55.645 --> 00:26:57.613
when the human body
just gives up.

00:26:57.647 --> 00:26:59.376
Yeah, well, maybe
my Doctor wasn't...

00:27:01.284 --> 00:27:02.751
Bashir to Infirmary.

00:27:02.785 --> 00:27:05.777
I need a nurse and an emergency
medkit here immediately.

00:27:07.623 --> 00:27:10.717
We finally were able
to localize the transporter beam

00:27:10.760 --> 00:27:12.819
and trace it back
to this location.

00:27:12.862 --> 00:27:15.228
These quarters have
been vacant for weeks.

00:27:15.264 --> 00:27:16.788
Somehow they overrode

00:27:16.832 --> 00:27:20.165
the security lock
on the door to gain access.

00:27:20.202 --> 00:27:21.328
So, what did they do?

00:27:21.370 --> 00:27:22.928
Bring in a portable transporter

00:27:23.039 --> 00:27:24.870
and beam
the surveillance equipment

00:27:24.907 --> 00:27:25.896
into the bulkhead?

00:27:25.942 --> 00:27:27.876
That was my first thought

00:27:27.910 --> 00:27:31.539
but then I realized
that a portable transporter

00:27:31.581 --> 00:27:33.714
is a rather large
and bulky piece of equipment

00:27:33.847 --> 00:27:35.781
to be carrying around the halls.

00:27:35.816 --> 00:27:36.805
That's true.

00:27:36.850 --> 00:27:41.719
So, then I began thinking
about...

00:27:43.890 --> 00:27:45.221
the replicator.

00:27:47.828 --> 00:27:51.127
Ah... they realigned
the matter-energy

00:27:51.164 --> 00:27:52.722
conversion matrix.

00:27:52.766 --> 00:27:55.530
Turning it
into a small transporter...

00:27:55.569 --> 00:28:00.404
a very sophisticated,
very professional job.

00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:02.704
So now we know
how they did it.

00:28:02.743 --> 00:28:04.370
The next question is who.

00:28:04.411 --> 00:28:07.505
I think I have the answer
to that as well.

00:28:10.550 --> 00:28:14.486
Now, this device is manufactured
on Davlos Ill...

00:28:14.521 --> 00:28:16.785
a planet on the Klingon border.

00:28:16.823 --> 00:28:19.314
In fact, Davlos does
over 90 percent

00:28:19.359 --> 00:28:21.190
of its trade
with the Klingon Empire.

00:28:21.228 --> 00:28:24.789
Oh, that's still very little
evidence to make an arrest.

00:28:24.831 --> 00:28:26.264
Yes, it is

00:28:26.299 --> 00:28:30.133
but then I contacted a friend
at Starfleet Intelligence

00:28:30.170 --> 00:28:33.571
who used to be assigned
to the Federation Embassy

00:28:33.607 --> 00:28:35.370
on the Klingon Homeworld.

00:28:35.408 --> 00:28:38.434
He put me in contact
with a former Klingon operative

00:28:38.478 --> 00:28:41.936
who is out of favor
with the current administration.

00:28:41.982 --> 00:28:44.610
This former operative
sent me a series of reports...

00:28:44.651 --> 00:28:45.618
Odo...

00:28:45.652 --> 00:28:47.142
cut to the chase.

00:28:47.187 --> 00:28:50.486
The three Klingons
now on the station

00:28:50.524 --> 00:28:53.960
are part
of a covert strike force

00:28:53.994 --> 00:28:57.361
that reports directly
to the Klingon High Council.

00:28:57.397 --> 00:28:58.921
Why didn't you just say so?

00:28:58.965 --> 00:29:01.593
Well, sometimes I have
to remind you

00:29:01.635 --> 00:29:03.398
just how good I am.

00:29:03.436 --> 00:29:06.234
Mm. So, Gowron sent
our three friends here

00:29:06.273 --> 00:29:08.468
and they're conducting
surveillance

00:29:08.508 --> 00:29:09.532
on the Romulan delegation.

00:29:09.576 --> 00:29:10.600
Why?

00:29:10.644 --> 00:29:12.339
Are they here to kill them?

00:29:12.379 --> 00:29:13.437
Possibly.

00:29:13.480 --> 00:29:15.414
It's also possible
that this is just

00:29:15.448 --> 00:29:17.882
a routine intelligence-
gathering operation.

00:29:17.918 --> 00:29:20.887
The high-energy laser
that killed O'Brien

00:29:20.921 --> 00:29:22.582
is simply a booby trap

00:29:22.622 --> 00:29:25.523
to prevent someone from
tampering with the device.

00:29:25.559 --> 00:29:27.459
It's not meant
for assassination.

00:29:27.494 --> 00:29:30.657
Well, in either case,
I think we have enough evidence

00:29:30.697 --> 00:29:33.427
to at least hold the Klingons
for questioning, don't you?

00:29:33.466 --> 00:29:34.558
Absolutely.

00:29:34.601 --> 00:29:36.660
And I think I can question them

00:29:36.703 --> 00:29:39.934
until the Romulan delegation
leaves the station.

00:29:40.040 --> 00:29:41.769
Just be careful.

00:29:42.976 --> 00:29:46.412
Commander,
there is no careful way

00:29:46.446 --> 00:29:48.778
to question a Klingon.

00:29:52.819 --> 00:29:55.287
I have...
I haven't given up.

00:29:56.456 --> 00:29:58.447
I won't give up.

00:29:58.491 --> 00:29:59.924
It's all right, Chief.

00:29:59.960 --> 00:30:01.291
You're okay.

00:30:04.231 --> 00:30:05.664
No, I'm not.

00:30:08.168 --> 00:30:11.968
You need to run
a basilar arterial scan.

00:30:12.038 --> 00:30:13.471
Why?

00:30:13.506 --> 00:30:14.803
Because if you don't

00:30:14.841 --> 00:30:17.833
I'm going to die
in less than five hours.

00:30:17.878 --> 00:30:19.345
Who told you that?

00:30:19.379 --> 00:30:22.212
You did.

00:30:22.249 --> 00:30:23.910
In the future.

00:30:25.018 --> 00:30:26.952
Oh.

00:30:26.987 --> 00:30:29.353
Well, who am I
to argue with me?

00:30:31.258 --> 00:30:32.247
Let me go!

00:30:33.526 --> 00:30:34.959
This is an outrage.

00:30:34.995 --> 00:30:36.257
We have done nothing.

00:30:39.065 --> 00:30:40.760
We will have our vengeance
on all of you for this.

00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:42.961
You are treating us
with dishonor.

00:30:43.003 --> 00:30:44.698
We have done nothing wrong.

00:30:44.738 --> 00:30:50.005
We take a very dim view of spies
and saboteurs on this station.

00:30:50.110 --> 00:30:51.577
Now you slander us.

00:30:51.611 --> 00:30:54.774
When my family finds out
what you have done

00:30:54.814 --> 00:30:57.248
they will come here
and kill you.

00:30:57.284 --> 00:30:58.808
I doubt that very much.

00:30:58.852 --> 00:31:01.480
The only people
who will be coming here

00:31:01.521 --> 00:31:04.251
are your friends
in Klingon Intelligence.

00:31:04.291 --> 00:31:06.088
And from what I understand

00:31:06.126 --> 00:31:09.289
they don't like being
embarrassed by operatives

00:31:09.329 --> 00:31:12.321
who fail in their missions.

00:31:12.365 --> 00:31:16.358
However, should you suddenly
feel like cooperating

00:31:16.403 --> 00:31:18.894
I may be persuaded
to let you go

00:31:18.939 --> 00:31:22.841
without contacting your friends
in Intelligence.

00:31:28.081 --> 00:31:30.311
May be.

00:31:42.696 --> 00:31:44.926
So how are you feeling, Chief?

00:31:44.965 --> 00:31:46.432
Better, sir.

00:31:46.466 --> 00:31:47.490
I've eliminated

00:31:47.534 --> 00:31:49.434
almost all the radioisotopes
from his body.

00:31:49.469 --> 00:31:50.868
Have to wait a couple more hours

00:31:50.904 --> 00:31:52.531
before I give him
the last treatment.

00:31:52.572 --> 00:31:54.938
But after that, there should be
no more timeshifting.

00:31:56.576 --> 00:31:58.305
What about
the quantum singularity?

00:31:58.345 --> 00:31:59.972
We've been able to track it

00:32:00.013 --> 00:32:02.573
by using its tetryon emissions
as a guide.

00:32:02.615 --> 00:32:04.947
It seems to be orbiting
Deep Space 9

00:32:05.051 --> 00:32:06.951
in a roughly elliptical fashion.

00:32:07.053 --> 00:32:10.147
At certain points in its orbit,
the singularity radiates

00:32:10.190 --> 00:32:12.715
temporal energy
at a specific wavelength.

00:32:12.759 --> 00:32:15.557
That seems to be
what triggers my time shifts.

00:32:15.595 --> 00:32:17.722
Is there any way
to break it out of its orbit

00:32:17.764 --> 00:32:18.924
and send it on its way?

00:32:18.965 --> 00:32:20.296
Well, we were hoping
to station...

00:32:22.168 --> 00:32:23.135
Come on, come on.

00:32:23.169 --> 00:32:24.534
Hurry up.
We don't have much time!

00:32:25.638 --> 00:32:27.071
Prepare to seal the hatch

00:32:27.107 --> 00:32:28.938
and release the docking clamps.

00:32:30.410 --> 00:32:31.672
Move quickly.
Let's go.

00:32:31.711 --> 00:32:34.305
All the way back.
Move quickly.

00:32:34.347 --> 00:32:35.439
Come on.

00:32:35.482 --> 00:32:38.474
Initiating emergency
escape protocol.

00:32:38.518 --> 00:32:41.078
Hang on,
I'm going to full impulse.

00:32:50.030 --> 00:32:51.554
Now what?

00:32:51.598 --> 00:32:53.088
You're here!

00:32:53.133 --> 00:32:54.998
Look, I don't know
what happened.

00:32:55.035 --> 00:32:58.095
I was asleep in bed when
the whole station was rocked

00:32:58.138 --> 00:32:59.332
by an explosion.

00:32:59.372 --> 00:33:02.773
Before I could get to Ops,
the evacuation alarm sounded.

00:33:02.809 --> 00:33:04.777
And the com systems were down.

00:33:04.811 --> 00:33:07.507
I got as many people
as I could in here.

00:33:07.547 --> 00:33:10.175
I don't know what happened
to the others.

00:33:10.216 --> 00:33:13.083
When you go back, you have
to find out what happened

00:33:13.119 --> 00:33:14.484
and stop it.

00:33:26.733 --> 00:33:28.598
My God!

00:33:32.672 --> 00:33:35.937
Chief, what's wrong?

00:33:35.975 --> 00:33:38.671
We've got a new problem, sir.

00:33:42.849 --> 00:33:44.783
Did you see anything
from the runabout

00:33:44.818 --> 00:33:47.412
that would indicate
how the station was destroyed?

00:33:47.454 --> 00:33:49.547
There were a series
of explosions

00:33:49.589 --> 00:33:51.989
that rippled across
the Habitat Ring.

00:33:52.025 --> 00:33:53.617
But it all happened so fast

00:33:53.660 --> 00:33:57.118
I couldn't get a clear sense
of exactly what was going on.

00:33:57.163 --> 00:34:00.098
Could you tell if you were
looking at internal explosions

00:34:00.133 --> 00:34:02.897
which might indicate some kind
of sabotage or accident

00:34:02.936 --> 00:34:05.200
or external explosions,
which might indicate

00:34:05.238 --> 00:34:06.432
we were under attack?

00:34:06.473 --> 00:34:08.600
No. No, I'm not sure.

00:34:08.641 --> 00:34:11.269
Do you remember seeing
any other ships nearby?

00:34:11.311 --> 00:34:14.144
No, but I had a very limited
view of the area.

00:34:14.180 --> 00:34:16.148
Well, it looks
like, at this point

00:34:16.182 --> 00:34:17.774
we can't rule anything out.

00:34:17.817 --> 00:34:19.307
Agreed.

00:34:20.653 --> 00:34:23.144
Make preparations
to evacuate the station.

00:34:23.189 --> 00:34:25.290
Do it quietly.

00:34:25.423 --> 00:34:27.254
If the destruction
of the station

00:34:27.292 --> 00:34:29.624
is the result
of an attack or sabotage

00:34:29.661 --> 00:34:31.561
we don't want
to alarm our enemy

00:34:31.596 --> 00:34:35.965
and make him trigger events
we're trying to avoid.

00:34:36.034 --> 00:34:38.434
Begin a complete systems check
of everything on the station

00:34:38.469 --> 00:34:40.630
that could potentially
cause this kind of explosion.

00:34:40.672 --> 00:34:41.866
Right.

00:34:41.906 --> 00:34:44.067
Commander...

00:34:44.108 --> 00:34:46.668
there might be another way
to find out what's going on.

00:34:46.711 --> 00:34:49.111
If I could travel
into the future again...

00:34:49.147 --> 00:34:52.446
this time just before
the destruction of DS9...

00:34:52.483 --> 00:34:54.713
I might be able to find out
what's going to happen

00:34:54.752 --> 00:34:56.310
then return to the present

00:34:56.354 --> 00:34:58.982
in time for us to prevent it
from happening.

00:34:59.090 --> 00:35:02.116
If you could flood my body
with high concentrations

00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:04.924
of delta-series radioisotopes,
it might trigger

00:35:05.029 --> 00:35:07.429
a time shift into the future.

00:35:07.465 --> 00:35:10.161
Possibly,
but those isotopes are toxic.

00:35:10.201 --> 00:35:12.669
It could cause permanent damage
to your nervous system.

00:35:12.704 --> 00:35:14.103
It might even kill you.

00:35:14.138 --> 00:35:17.904
Well, if the future happens
the way I saw it happen

00:35:17.942 --> 00:35:19.876
a lot of people are
going to get killed

00:35:19.911 --> 00:35:21.173
when the station explodes.

00:35:21.212 --> 00:35:22.839
It's a risk I'm willing to take.

00:35:22.880 --> 00:35:25.348
Even if you're able
to initiate a time jump

00:35:25.383 --> 00:35:27.817
each time you traveled
into the future

00:35:27.852 --> 00:35:29.843
you've always gone five hours.

00:35:29.887 --> 00:35:32.788
How do you propose to shorten
the length of a jump?

00:35:32.824 --> 00:35:35.657
Well, there might be a link
between the temporal frequency

00:35:35.693 --> 00:35:36.819
of the singularity

00:35:36.861 --> 00:35:38.954
and the length
of the time shift.

00:35:38.996 --> 00:35:42.227
We might be able to calibrate

00:35:42.266 --> 00:35:43.961
the decay constant
of the isotope

00:35:44.068 --> 00:35:45.365
that we inject you with

00:35:45.403 --> 00:35:47.337
to match the frequency
of the singularity.

00:35:47.372 --> 00:35:48.862
And with a few minor adjustments

00:35:48.906 --> 00:35:50.339
we can control
how far you jump

00:35:50.375 --> 00:35:51.342
into the future.

00:35:51.376 --> 00:35:52.604
Exactly.

00:35:54.312 --> 00:35:55.472
All right.

00:35:55.513 --> 00:35:57.981
But if you can't do it
within two hours

00:35:58.049 --> 00:36:00.882
I'm going to begin
to evacuate the station.

00:36:00.918 --> 00:36:02.283
Understood.

00:36:09.494 --> 00:36:11.826
Now, when you activate
this device

00:36:11.863 --> 00:36:14.855
it'll inject you with a two-rad
dose of delta isotopes.

00:36:14.899 --> 00:36:16.059
Now, if our calculations
are right

00:36:16.100 --> 00:36:17.931
that should put you about
three hours into the future.

00:36:18.035 --> 00:36:19.525
What's the margin of error?

00:36:19.570 --> 00:36:21.060
Plus or minus half an hour,
I'd say.

00:36:21.105 --> 00:36:22.436
But that's the best we could do.

00:36:22.473 --> 00:36:24.338
Now, it's already set
for the return trip.

00:36:24.375 --> 00:36:26.309
So all you have to do
is activate it again

00:36:26.344 --> 00:36:27.709
to return to the present.

00:36:27.745 --> 00:36:28.712
Right.

00:36:28.746 --> 00:36:31.544
And remember,
don't wait too long.

00:36:31.582 --> 00:36:33.049
Your body will be experiencing

00:36:33.084 --> 00:36:34.949
symptoms
of severe radiation poisoning.

00:36:34.986 --> 00:36:37.955
If you don't get treatment,
it will kill you.

00:36:37.989 --> 00:36:39.923
I won't forget.

00:36:39.957 --> 00:36:41.049
Good.

00:36:42.860 --> 00:36:44.293
Julian, there's a...

00:36:44.328 --> 00:36:46.626
a message in my quarters
for Keiko if...

00:36:46.664 --> 00:36:49.258
I understand, Miles.

00:37:16.127 --> 00:37:17.492
0200.

00:37:19.430 --> 00:37:22.194
That's three and a half hours
into the future.

00:37:30.842 --> 00:37:32.810
Miles, Miles!

00:37:32.844 --> 00:37:33.902
Wake up!

00:37:33.945 --> 00:37:36.038
What?

00:37:36.080 --> 00:37:37.570
Computer, lights.

00:37:42.753 --> 00:37:45.347
Oh, no, not you again.

00:37:46.824 --> 00:37:48.052
What is it now?

00:37:48.092 --> 00:37:49.184
Listen to me.

00:37:49.227 --> 00:37:51.252
I've jumped ahead
and seen your future.

00:37:51.295 --> 00:37:54.560
Don't ask me how,
it'll take too long to explain.

00:37:54.599 --> 00:37:57.932
There's going to be a disaster.

00:37:57.969 --> 00:38:00.335
DS9 will be destroyed.

00:38:01.939 --> 00:38:03.236
Destroyed? How?

00:38:03.274 --> 00:38:04.434
I don't know.

00:38:04.475 --> 00:38:05.703
That's why I'm here.

00:38:05.743 --> 00:38:08.610
I have to find out
what's going to happen

00:38:08.646 --> 00:38:13.242
and then travel back
into the past and prevent it.

00:38:16.254 --> 00:38:17.653
You look pretty bad.

00:38:17.688 --> 00:38:21.385
It's the radiation.

00:38:21.425 --> 00:38:24.360
Well, if you feel bad
and you're my past self

00:38:24.395 --> 00:38:26.158
shouldn't I feel bad, too?

00:38:28.232 --> 00:38:30.666
I hate temporal mechanics.

00:38:32.470 --> 00:38:34.938
Let's get down to Ops
and see what's going on.

00:38:40.444 --> 00:38:42.139
Help me up.

00:38:53.024 --> 00:38:55.652
Run a sensor sweep
of the entire station.

00:38:55.693 --> 00:38:58.287
Look for anything
that might indicate a...

00:38:59.430 --> 00:39:00.988
Report!

00:39:01.032 --> 00:39:03.000
A Romulan warbird just
de-cloaked off of Lower Pylon 2.

00:39:03.034 --> 00:39:05.229
They've taken out
our shield generators.

00:39:05.269 --> 00:39:06.566
On screen.

00:39:09.140 --> 00:39:12.075
Lock phasers and return fire.

00:39:13.544 --> 00:39:15.375
They've hit the fusion reactor.

00:39:15.413 --> 00:39:16.471
Main power's down.

00:39:16.514 --> 00:39:18.914
Defense systems off-line.

00:39:18.950 --> 00:39:22.716
Try to reroute phasers through
the emergency power couplings.

00:39:26.057 --> 00:39:27.615
Miles, you've got your answer.

00:39:27.658 --> 00:39:29.023
The quantum singularity

00:39:29.060 --> 00:39:31.051
that's been orbiting
the station...

00:39:31.095 --> 00:39:32.187
it's the Romulans.

00:39:32.229 --> 00:39:33.924
Are you listening?

00:39:33.965 --> 00:39:35.523
The Romulans use

00:39:35.566 --> 00:39:37.864
a confined singularity
to power their warp core.

00:39:37.902 --> 00:39:39.460
That's what we've
been detecting.

00:39:39.503 --> 00:39:41.334
That's what's causing
the time shifts.

00:39:41.372 --> 00:39:42.634
You must go back and tell them

00:39:42.673 --> 00:39:46.234
to put up the shields
and stand by for an attack.

00:39:46.277 --> 00:39:49.405
I can't.

00:39:49.447 --> 00:39:52.439
I can't get through
another shift.

00:39:52.483 --> 00:39:55.077
It's the radiation poisoning,
it...

00:39:59.757 --> 00:40:01.281
You go.

00:40:01.325 --> 00:40:03.122
Just activate it.

00:40:03.160 --> 00:40:06.220
It's set for the return trip.

00:40:06.263 --> 00:40:07.787
Me?

00:40:07.832 --> 00:40:09.322
I don't belong there.

00:40:09.367 --> 00:40:11.927
I'm you... you're me...

00:40:11.969 --> 00:40:14.938
It does... doesn't matter.

00:40:14.972 --> 00:40:16.200
Just go.

00:40:18.175 --> 00:40:19.164
Go!

00:40:37.628 --> 00:40:38.993
Chief!

00:40:39.063 --> 00:40:40.052
What happened?

00:40:41.232 --> 00:40:43.723
It worked.

00:40:43.768 --> 00:40:44.894
O'Brien to Sisko.

00:40:44.935 --> 00:40:46.368
Go ahead, Chief.

00:40:46.404 --> 00:40:49.271
I've been to the future,
Commander.

00:40:49.306 --> 00:40:51.604
The quantum singularity
off the station

00:40:51.642 --> 00:40:54.634
is actually in the warp core
of a cloaked Romulan warbird.

00:40:54.679 --> 00:40:57.614
They're going to de-cloak and
fire on us in a matter of hours.

00:40:57.648 --> 00:40:59.479
Understood, Chief.

00:40:59.517 --> 00:41:00.984
Raise shields.

00:41:01.018 --> 00:41:02.918
Stand by weapons systems.

00:41:02.953 --> 00:41:05.888
I don't understand it.

00:41:05.923 --> 00:41:08.756
Your body should be flooded
with delta-series radiation

00:41:08.793 --> 00:41:11.125
but there's only a tiny
amount in your tissues.

00:41:11.162 --> 00:41:13.756
Your metabolic readings
are different.

00:41:13.798 --> 00:41:14.765
What happened?

00:41:14.799 --> 00:41:18.901
There's been a... a change.

00:41:21.203 --> 00:41:25.196
Uh... I really have
nothing else to say.

00:41:25.240 --> 00:41:27.208
I think you're lying, Quark.

00:41:27.242 --> 00:41:28.732
About what part?

00:41:28.777 --> 00:41:30.108
All of it.

00:41:30.145 --> 00:41:31.772
Well, at least I'm consistent.

00:41:34.016 --> 00:41:36.382
Quark, you can leave.

00:41:37.386 --> 00:41:39.217
Thank you.

00:41:43.525 --> 00:41:46.983
I know you have a cloaked
warbird orbiting the station.

00:41:47.062 --> 00:41:49.326
And I know that you're
planning an attack.

00:41:49.364 --> 00:41:51.423
At first, I couldn't
understand why

00:41:51.466 --> 00:41:52.694
and then I remembered

00:41:52.734 --> 00:41:54.463
what you said
about the Dominion...

00:41:54.503 --> 00:41:57.404
how they were the greatest
threat to the Alpha Quadrant

00:41:57.439 --> 00:41:58.701
in the last century.

00:41:58.740 --> 00:42:00.401
If you really believed that

00:42:00.442 --> 00:42:02.307
then the only way you
could ever be truly safe

00:42:02.344 --> 00:42:05.313
from the Dominion would be
to collapse the wormhole.

00:42:05.347 --> 00:42:07.076
But you knew we wouldn't
just sit by

00:42:07.115 --> 00:42:08.446
and watch while you did it.

00:42:08.483 --> 00:42:10.383
So you had to destroy
the station, too.

00:42:10.419 --> 00:42:13.445
That way,
there'd be no witnesses.

00:42:13.488 --> 00:42:16.457
Everyone would assume
that Deep Space 9 was destroyed

00:42:16.491 --> 00:42:19.051
by what appeared to be
the accidental collapse

00:42:19.094 --> 00:42:20.618
of the wormhole.

00:42:20.662 --> 00:42:22.323
An interesting...

00:42:22.364 --> 00:42:24.696
theory, Commander.

00:42:24.733 --> 00:42:27.167
But that's all it is,
a theory.

00:42:27.202 --> 00:42:28.726
That's right.

00:42:28.770 --> 00:42:30.965
But I'll tell you
what's not a theory.

00:42:31.073 --> 00:42:34.600
We tracked the tetryon emissions
back to your warbird

00:42:34.643 --> 00:42:37.669
and I have about 50 photon
torpedoes locked onto it

00:42:37.713 --> 00:42:39.840
right now.

00:42:50.859 --> 00:42:52.884
I think it's time we left.

00:42:52.928 --> 00:42:54.395
I couldn't agree more.

00:42:54.429 --> 00:42:57.626
Constable, will you please
escort our... guests

00:42:57.666 --> 00:42:59.793
to the nearest transporter room?

00:42:59.835 --> 00:43:01.826
If you'll come with me.

00:43:18.120 --> 00:43:20.554
So you're telling me
that you remember

00:43:20.589 --> 00:43:23.217
playing this game
with me in the future?

00:43:23.258 --> 00:43:24.247
Right.

00:43:25.527 --> 00:43:28.963
All right, what am I
going to hit?

00:43:29.031 --> 00:43:31.397
20, outer ring.

00:43:37.039 --> 00:43:38.529
Why, that's remarkable.

00:43:38.573 --> 00:43:40.438
It's also a little disturbing.

00:43:40.475 --> 00:43:44.775
I have this nagging feeling
that I don't really belong here.

00:43:44.813 --> 00:43:46.508
This isn't really my life.

00:43:46.548 --> 00:43:48.209
You know, maybe this life

00:43:48.250 --> 00:43:50.616
belongs
to that other Miles O'Brien.

00:43:50.652 --> 00:43:52.517
Listen, Chief, whether you
are living in the past

00:43:52.554 --> 00:43:53.987
or the present,
you are Miles O'Brien.

00:43:54.056 --> 00:43:55.819
The only difference is
you have a few memories

00:43:55.857 --> 00:43:56.915
the other one didn't have.

00:43:59.294 --> 00:44:01.819
Well, I think I'll go to bed.

00:44:01.863 --> 00:44:03.922
I'm still kind of tired.

00:44:03.999 --> 00:44:06.297
Now, that sounds
like a good idea.

00:44:08.970 --> 00:44:10.904
Quark.

00:44:10.939 --> 00:44:12.770
Dabo.

00:44:12.808 --> 00:44:14.639
Dabo?

00:44:14.676 --> 00:44:15.870
Dabo!

00:44:19.815 --> 00:44:22.648
Wait, Chief, wait!
